### SmartChat API examples
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (Huachao Mao) and click
### "Send Request" above each request. Start the app first: docker compose up -d, then ./mvnw spring-boot:run

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Register Alice (only needed once; 409 Conflict afterwards is fine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 2. Register Bob (only needed once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 3. Log in as Alice (run this before the requests that use her token)
# @name loginAlice
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 4. Log in as Bob
# @name loginBob
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

@aliceToken = {{loginAlice.response.body.$.token}}
@bobToken = {{loginBob.response.body.$.token}}

### 5. Who am I? (Alice)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 6. Who am I? (Bob) - his id is used by the DM request below
# @name meBob
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### 7. Who is online? (users with an open WebSocket connection; [] until a client connects)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/online
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 8. Alice's rooms (new users are added to #general)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 9. Alice creates a private room
# @name privateRoom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Project X",
  "description": "Only invited people",
  "isPrivate": true
}

### 10. Bob can't see it (404), because private rooms are hidden from non-members
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{privateRoom.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### 11. Bob asks to join, which notifies Alice
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{privateRoom.response.body.$.id}}/join
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### 12. Alice sees the pending request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{privateRoom.response.body.$.id}}/join-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 13. Alice sends Bob a DM. Send this 21+ times within 10 seconds to hit the rate limit (429)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dm
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "receiverId": {{meBob.response.body.$.id}},
  "content": "Hi Bob!"
}

### 13b. Unread counts per room for Bob ({ roomId: count }); updated by the Kafka consumer
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/unread
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### 13c. Bob opens #general (room 1), resetting its unread count
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/1/read
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### 14. Bob's unread notifications
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/unread
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### 15. Error format check: unknown room -> 404 ProblemDetail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 16. No token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/mine
